# The environment of the platform.
#
# The platform is three services. Each of them reads its own variables,
# and each of them has its own file:
#
#   packages/gateway/.env.example   Gateway   (GATEWAY_*)
#   packages/access/.env.example    Access    (ACCESS_*)
#   packages/data/.env.example      Data      (DATA_*)
#
# This file is the index of them: it names the three groups and it says
# which service reads which one. Copy the file of a service to a `.env`
# of that service and adjust it.
#
# The file `.env.min` of the root is the shortest of them: it holds the
# variables a stack of `deploy/compose` refuses to start without, with
# the example values of a development machine.
#
# Every value has a default in the runtime of its service, except the ones
# a production deployment has to set: the service refuses to start
# without them.
#
# This file holds no credential. A secret belongs in the secret store of
# the platform, never in the repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gateway (packages/gateway/.env.example)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The route table, the identity provider, Access, the shared
# state, the sessions, the limits and the operations.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access (packages/access/.env.example)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The issuer, the database, the shared store, the tokens of the
# administration and of the decisions, and the key that signs the tokens.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data (packages/data/.env.example)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The database, the role of the api, the bindings of the gateway, the
# manifests of the deployment, the access context of Access
# and the key that signs the cursors.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The console (packages/console/.env.example)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The listener, the client of Access, the gateway, the
# credential of the administration and the secret of the sessions.
